\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Applying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-5c06c612e0c8fb43f1f578d124b67093\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/5c06c612e0c8fb43f1f578d124b67093\"></div></div></div>",
